{"metadata":{"title":"Mystery of the Clock Tower","author":"AI","language":"English","difficulty":"A2"},"content":[["The old town","of Blackwood","had a secret.","In the center","stood a tall","stone clock tower.","For fifty years,","the clock","did not work.","The hands","pointed forever","at midnight."],["A young detective","named Arthur","arrived on Tuesday.","He heard","strange noises","coming from","the high tower.","People whispered","about ghosts","living inside.","Arthur did not","believe in ghosts."],["He found","the heavy wooden door","unlocked today.","He pushed","it open slowly.","Dust fell down","from the ceiling.","He climbed","the spiral stairs.","Every step","made a loud","creaking sound."],["At the top,","he discovered","a small room.","There were","many books","on the floor.","An old man","sat near","the giant gears.","The man was","fixing the clock","with great care."],["Arthur asked,","Who are you?","The old man","smiled kindly","and replied,","I am the keeper","of lost time.","I stopped","the clocks","long ago","to save","this peaceful town."],["Suddenly,","the heavy bell","began to ring.","Bong, bong,","it echoed loudly.","The time","moved forward","once again.","Arthur smiled","at the watchmaker.","It was","a wonderful mystery."]]}